BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 268.0 Td (      In ancient times, two rivers flowed through separate valleys-the River of Giving and the R) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 258.0 Td (        iver of Return. Each was guarded by a spirit who possessed five golden seeds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 248.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 238.0 Td (      The Spirit of Giving discovered a sacred truth: any seed planted in the other's valley wou) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 228.0 Td (        ld bloom threefold. But to plant required crossing the treacherous mountain, relinquishi) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 218.0 Td (        ng the seed forever into another's care.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 208.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 198.0 Td (      The Spirit of Return, upon receiving these miraculous blooms, faced a choice: keep all fif) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 188.0 Td (        teen flowers, or return some across the mountain to honor the trust placed in them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 178.0 Td (      ) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 168.0 Td (      At first, the Spirit of Giving sent nothing, fearing loss. Both valleys remained barren. T) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.0 Tf 48.0 158.0 Td (        hen, tentatively, they sent one seed. It became three flowers. The Spirit of Return, mov) Tj ET
